 have reached `origin`);\n2. pytest fails in ~50s on several changes, fast enough to be a collection/import error, and it does NOT reproduce locally.\n\nDo NOT close this ticket until its change is Verified +1 and merged. A subagent is driving the stack to green; a session-only cron loop (46e3b0eb) is harvesting reviews, landing green changes and closing merged tickets.\n\nNote for whoever lands this: amend only with `git commit --amend --no-edit`. Re-committing a change that already carries a Change-Id opens a DUPLICATE Gerrit change — that is how change 2534 came to exist and be abandoned.","timestamp":1788398763289796001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788317659321436001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b8c66b97-88db-4cf6-820b-1a57166f16bb","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"},{"link_uuid":"8f9b9e6a-606e-42ec-9c7b-2f6e9b93df9f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c37-ac69-ce9e-41b8"},{"link_uuid":"34abdd22-c858-4cff-b1f6-f2cc97cab764","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8f46-01f4-267d-4643"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F7 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), MEDIUM.\n\n## Problem\n\n- `src/rebar/types.py:23` `TicketType` (7 values) — canonical\n- `src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:41` `_TYPES` — the same 7, hand-copied, plus a prose copy in\n  `_USAGE`\n\n`composer` is the OUTLIER: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py:119` already derives the\nsame vocabulary as `frozenset(get_args(TicketType))`. A type added to `TicketType` but not to\n`_TYPES` is rejected at `create`, so the new type cannot be filed at all.\n\n## Approach — generate-from-canonical\n\nCopy the sibling derivation. `rebar.types` imports only `typing`, so there is no cycle.\n\nThis ticket adds its own `from rebar.types import TicketType` — it does NOT depend on F3\n(`contiguous-industrial-dugong`) having landed first. An earlier revision of this plan claimed\ncomposer already imported from `rebar.types` \"after the F3 consolidation\"; that was read from\nan unmerged working tree and is not true of `origin/main`, which is the basis a review pins.\nThe two changes touch adjacent lines but neither requires the other.\n\nThe `_USAGE` prose copy is regenerated from the same set rather than re-typed, so help text and\nvalidation cannot disagree.\n\nDistinct from F3 (`contiguous-industrial-dugong`), which consolidated the plan-review EXEMPTION\nsubset. This is the full create vocabulary — a different concept that happens to live next door,\nwhich is why F3 deliberately left it alone.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `_TYPES` is derived from `TicketType`. Verified by a test asserting equality with\n      `frozenset(get_args(TicketType))` and the literal being gone.\n- [x] AC2: the `_USAGE` help text lists the same vocabulary, generated not re-typed. Verified by a\n      test asserting every member appears in `_USAGE` and that no non-member does.\n- [x] AC3: a type added to `TicketType` becomes creatable with no second edit. Verified by a test\n      driving the validation path with the derived set.\n- [x] AC4: `create` still rejects a genuinely unknown type. Verified by the existing composer suite\n      plus an explicit rejection test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"composer or create\" -q` — AC1-AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"derive _TYPES from TicketType and generate the usage text from it"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_composer_type_vocabulary.py","reason":"the oracle"},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"TICKET_TYPES is emitted here; composer consumes it as the single master"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/gen_types.py","reason":"types.py is GENERATED, so the constant must be emitted by the generator to survive regeneration"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","ma